1
00:00:03,004 --> 00:00:14,616
This is the order board of a plant that converts flexible packaging: every open order, every step, against the date the customer was given.

2
00:00:14,938 --> 00:00:24,327
Lamination, curing, slitting, bag making. Each step shows whether it is planned, running, done or behind plan.

3
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:36,026
Bag maker 2 stood still from Friday noon until this morning. The two orders queued on it are now late, one by a day, the other by three.

4
00:00:36,349 --> 00:00:46,571
The last column says how far each date can be trusted: confirmed data, ERP data nobody has checked yet, or an assumption.

5
00:00:47,757 --> 00:00:56,819
A customer calls: 60,000 vacuum bags, wanted in ten days. Sales enters the order as the customer gives it.

6
00:00:57,141 --> 00:01:03,437
One click, and today's plan answers with a date: on the requested day.

7
00:01:03,759 --> 00:01:14,902
With every reason: PE film is short and a purchase arrives on Thursday. Then lamination, 48 hours of curing, slitting and bag making.

8
00:01:15,225 --> 00:01:22,596
The date rests on one assumption: nobody has confirmed the speed of bag maker 1 yet.

9
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:27,441
Planning confirms it, and the date turns green.

10
00:01:27,762 --> 00:01:37,054
Sales confirms the order. Its steps join the machine queues, the ERP is told, and the customer gets the date.

11
00:01:38,204 --> 00:01:44,498
This is the confirmation the customer received, in their own language.

12
00:01:46,468 --> 00:01:53,687
Machine load over two weeks. The new order sits at the end of bag maker 1's queue.

13
00:01:54,008 --> 00:02:00,460
On bag maker 2, the job held up by the stop pushes everything behind it.

14
00:02:06,805 --> 00:02:14,790
At the machine, the operator sees the job on it and the next ones, in the order of the plan.

15
00:02:15,114 --> 00:02:21,866
The bag maker finishes its job: 60,000 bags. That was the order's last step.

16
00:02:22,187 --> 00:02:27,791
The order is ready, and the customer is told the same minute.

17
00:02:28,945 --> 00:02:33,304
On the board, the order is ready to ship.

18
00:02:33,626 --> 00:02:45,231
Built on the plant's own data: orders and stock from its ERP, machines and rules confirmed by its people. One process first, then the next.
